# DURABLE REPRO for `todo/t1373` — `Box[T].get()` through a STRUCT-FIELD
# receiver is SILENT-WRONG ON THE DEFAULT BACKEND.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at pristine HEAD and unchanged by R50 Track A2):
#     C     → prints garbage (a pointer value, e.g. 187651060765344), rc 0
#     LLVM  → prints 9, rc 0
# `gg check` is clean, both builds are rc 0, and ASan reports nothing.
#
# MECHANISM, read off the emitted C rather than inferred — two call-emit shapes
# for the same operation, one of them deref-correct:
#     __v8  = &s.b;                                 /* the FIELD'S ADDRESS   */
#     __v10 = Box__Box__int64_t__get(__v8);         /* to a BY-VALUE __get   */
#     __v12 = Box__int64_t__get(*(Box__int64_t*)__v11);   /* sibling derefs  */
#
# ⚠ THIS INVERTS A FILED MEASUREMENT, AND THAT IS THE POINT. `todo/t0685`
# records `Box[int].get()` as green on both backends — TRUE FOR A LOCAL
# RECEIVER, FALSE FOR A FIELD ONE. The axis `t0685` enumerates is the PAYLOAD
# TYPE; the axis that actually discriminates is the RECEIVER PLACE. A fixture set
# sampling only local receivers is an anecdote on the axis that matters
# (Core #12). Do not merge this into `t0685` or `t0684` — a fix aimed at payload
# types leaves it alive.
#
# ⚠ WHY IT IS FILED HERE RATHER THAN ABSORBED BY R50 TRACK A2 — and the claim
# is about THIS PROGRAM'S INVARIANCE, not about the newtype's. Measured on both
# backends, at pristine HEAD and after A2's fix:
#
#     program / read shape          PRE C     PRE LLVM   POST C     POST LLVM
#     THIS FILE   s.b.get()         garbage   9          garbage    9
#     struct      *(s.b)            9         9          9          9
#     newtype     n.0.get()         rc 1      rc 1       garbage    9
#     newtype     *(n.0)            rc 1      rc 1       9          9
#
# THIS PROGRAM IS BYTE-INVARIANT ACROSS A2 — pristine HEAD, every partial
# revert, and the full fix all print the same garbage on C and the same 9 on
# LLVM. THAT INVARIANCE IS THE WHOLE ARGUMENT: A2 cannot have caused a
# wrongness that predates it and that its patch does not move.
#
# ⚠ AND NOTE WHAT THE TABLE DOES *NOT* SAY. The newtype rows are rc 1 at PRE,
# so newtype and struct are NOT alike at pristine HEAD — A2 is what brings the
# newtype up to the struct's behaviour, exactly (garbage/9 under `.get()`,
# 9/9 under `*`). An earlier draft of this comment claimed the two matched "at
# every state including pristine HEAD"; that was false, and the corrected
# statement is the stronger one: A2 REACHES parity, and the residual C garbage
# under `.get()` is a property both shapes inherit from the defect below.
#
# INTENDED (asserted by the `#[ignore]`d test): `9` on C and on LLVM.
# Un-ignore when the field-receiver call emit derefs like its sibling.
struct SB:
    Box[int] b

void main():
    Box[int] bb = Box(9)
    SB s = SB(^bb)
    print(s.b.get())
